{%- comment -%}
  The Dog Nook — robots.txt

  ⚠️ Adding this file makes the THEME responsible for robots.txt. Shopify's own
  rules are preserved by looping `robots.default_groups` first and emitting them
  unchanged — never replace that loop with hand-written rules, or you lose
  Shopify's checkout/cart/account protections and risk de-indexing the shop.

  What this file adds: explicit permission for AI answer engines. Without a named
  group these bots fall under `User-agent: *`; naming them is what lets us opt in
  deliberately (Google-Extended and Applebot-Extended in particular are pure
  opt-in tokens — silence means "no"). Being quotable in ChatGPT, Claude,
  Perplexity and AI Overviews is the fastest visibility route for a domain with
  no authority yet, which is why this matters more than usual here.

  Each AI group repeats the private-path disallows rather than only `Allow: /`,
  because robots.txt precedence gives a named group priority over `*` — so a bare
  Allow would invite them into /cart and /checkout.

  Verify after deploying: fetch https://thedognook.co.uk/robots.txt and confirm
  the default groups still appear above the AI section.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% for group in robots.default_groups %}
{{ group.user_agent }}
{% for rule in group.rules %}{{ rule }}
{% endfor %}{% if group.sitemap != blank %}{{ group.sitemap }}
{% endif %}{% endfor %}
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# AI answer engines — explicitly welcome on public content.
# Removing a line here withdraws consent for that engine.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
{% assign ai_agents = 'GPTBot,OAI-SearchBot,ChatGPT-User,ClaudeBot,Claude-User,Claude-SearchBot,PerplexityBot,Perplexity-User,Google-Extended,Applebot-Extended,Amazonbot,meta-externalagent,CCBot' | split: ',' %}
{% for agent in ai_agents %}User-agent: {{ agent }}
Disallow: /admin
Disallow: /cart
Disallow: /checkout
Disallow: /orders
Disallow: /account
Disallow: /search
Allow: /

{% endfor %}Sitemap: {{ shop.url }}/sitemap.xml
